# TOKA parity manifest — the recorded outcome class of every toka case in each
# executor of the differential square (ref, clingo, Drools), pinned so gate 11
# (scripts/check-toka-parity.sh) fails on any drift. Derived by the slotmeting
# method (backlog/done/20260826-toka-slotmeting.md): each scenario is a slice of
# the ©-Belastingdienst TOKA casus (companions resolved to an ir.json), replayed
# against the hand-derived case.json. This file, the slices and the cases live
# ONLY here under toka/ (the charter zone); ©-material never leaves it.
#
# Columns, pipe-delimited: scenario | ref | clingo | clingo-fragment | drools | drools-fragment
#   ref     = PASS   : the ref-100 oracle matches every pinned expectation (exit 0). A wrong
#                      value makes the runner exit non-zero -> the gate reddens (no silent divergence).
#   clingo  = PASS   : clingo's stable model matches the same pinned expectations (exit 0), OR
#           = FAULT  : clingo refuses LOUDLY at translation; the fragment MUST appear in its output.
#   drools  = PLAYED : the uchar-IR-loading Drools backend lowered every form and matched, OR
#           = EXCLUDE : a form the v0 backend does not carry is refused LOUDLY per form; the
#                      fragment MUST appear. Every toka slice bundles the whole structural model,
#                      including the wederkerig Partnerrelatie feittype (§13.3.9.2), so the backend
#                      refuses each slice up front; toka-28 additionally carries an objectcreatie
#                      (§13.4.6), checked first. A FAIL/ERROR (a value difference without a fault)
#                      is NEVER listed and always reddens the gate — the hard zero-silent-divergence rule.
scenario-toka-17-bepaal-leeftijd|PASS|PASS|-|EXCLUDE|wederkerig self-relation (§13.3.9.2)
